# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Cast Shock and choose the opposing player through the visible controls.
# Forcing: The starting position offers the named interaction without drawing or building a board.
# AI behavior: An empty hand and battlefield leave no competing actions.
# Failure modes: Wrong targets, missing actions or incorrect results fail the browser assertions.
# Card roles: Hand and battlefield cards supply only the tested action and its mana. Library lands prevent decking.
# Protocol path: Real legal actions, player responses and authoritative game-state updates.
